``` KV-02 | KV Store Replication Lag Between SHC Members
    Splunk Administrator Field Manual - Gaurav Malik

    Use case: KV Store-backed lookups return different results depending on
    which search head serves the request; measure replication lag across the
    SHC replica set and identify the stale member.
    Run on: SH, with _introspection from every SHC member. The KV Store
    replica set stats are sampled on each member.
    Query: Main query
    STATUS: lab verification pending; field or message names may differ on your version.
```
index=_introspection sourcetype=kvstore component=KVStoreReplicaSetStats
    earliest=-1h
| spath path=data.members{} output=member
| mvexpand member
| spath input=member path=name output=member_name
| spath input=member path=stateStr output=state
| spath input=member path=optimeDate output=optime_raw
| eval optime=coalesce(strptime(optime_raw, "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.%3N%Z"),
                       tonumber(optime_raw) / 1000)
| eventstats max(eval(if(state="PRIMARY", optime, null()))) as primary_optime
        by _time host
| eval lag_s=round(primary_optime - optime, 1)
| stats latest(state) as state max(lag_s) as max_lag_s avg(lag_s) as avg_lag_s
        by member_name
| eval avg_lag_s=round(avg_lag_s, 1)
| sort - max_lag_s
